WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

2
00:02:30.263 --> 00:02:33.549
Standing in the door.
l could see. . .

3
00:02:33.725 --> 00:02:35.801
. . .the lights on a drop zone.

4
00:02:35.977 --> 00:02:41.103
And l had to assume that was
our drop zone. way ahead of us.

5
00:02:41.275 --> 00:02:43.896
And. . . .

6
00:02:44.069 --> 00:02:47.320
So we had the red light.

7
00:02:47.489 --> 00:02:51.274
l had everybody standing up.
ready to jump.

8
00:02:51.452 --> 00:02:55.450
So when the plane started
to get hit. and suddenly. . .

9
00:02:55.623 --> 00:02:59.835
. . .the pilot gives me the green light.
l'm out the door.

10
00:03:00.003 --> 00:03:05.044
Got such an opening blast
or opening shot from the prop blast. . .

11
00:03:05.216 --> 00:03:11.220
. . .that it broke this chinstrap
that we had on the helmet liner.

12
00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:15.553
That's when l lost this famous leg bag
everybody talks about.

13
00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:21.434
Just from the shock of the opening.
lt just flew right off my foot.

14
00:03:21.609 --> 00:03:24.182
We came from the sky.

15
00:03:24.362 --> 00:03:30.696
We hit. and in any direction you went.
there would be enemy. You knew it.

16
00:03:30.868 --> 00:03:34.403
And that was all part of what
you accepted.

17
00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:38.329
How do you prepare yourself mentally?

18
00:03:38.502 --> 00:03:41.538
Each man must do that himself.

19
00:03:41.713 --> 00:03:45.711
Each man must prepare
himself mentally. . .

20
00:03:45.884 --> 00:03:48.802
. . .to make that jump.

21
00:03:48.971 --> 00:03:53.099
ln the back of your mind.
you wonder what's gonna happen.

22
00:03:53.267 --> 00:03:56.387
You know you've been trained
and trained. . .

23
00:03:56.562 --> 00:04:00.643
. . .and what your job is
and what you're supposed to do.

24
00:04:00.817 --> 00:04:06.772
That's what you gotta think about.
We lost a lot of people that night.

25
00:04:06.948 --> 00:04:12.903
But you try to put
it all out of your mind.

26
00:05:07.554 --> 00:05:09.712
Smith!

27
00:05:09.889 --> 00:05:12.641
Give me a light.

28
00:05:42.591 --> 00:05:45.461
Lip! Did Evans make it?

29
00:05:45.635 --> 00:05:50.594
Yes. sir.
He's in Lt. Meehan's stick. sir.

30
00:05:58.649 --> 00:06:02.018
Lt. Meehan. Lt. Meehan.

31
00:06:02.194 --> 00:06:05.196
Will could use some help.

32
00:06:12.664 --> 00:06:14.242
Will!

33
00:06:14.416 --> 00:06:17.701
Will. hey! Will!
l need your help here.

34
00:07:49.099 --> 00:07:51.720
Get ready!

35
00:07:51.893 --> 00:07:54.219
Stand up!

36
00:07:55.314 --> 00:07:57.353
Hook up!

37
00:07:59.318 --> 00:08:02.438
Equipment check!

38
00:08:06.659 --> 00:08:09.909
-Sound off for equipment check!
-Ten okay!

39
00:08:10.079 --> 00:08:12.119
-Nine okay!
-Eight okay!

40
00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:13.950
-Seven okay!
-Six okay!

41
00:08:14.125 --> 00:08:15.833
-Five okay!
-Four okay!

42
00:08:16.002 --> 00:08:17.995
-Three okay!
-Two okay!

43
00:08:18.171 --> 00:08:19.499
One okay!

44
00:08:55.252 --> 00:08:57.494
Jesus Christ!
Let's go. let's go!

45
00:08:57.671 --> 00:09:01.087
-Does that light look green to you?
-Let's go!

46
00:09:01.258 --> 00:09:03.583
l'm hit!

47
00:09:14.981 --> 00:09:19.109
Jesus! Tell Meehan
to get them out of there!

48
00:09:30.372 --> 00:09:32.329
Two o'clock!

49
00:09:32.499 --> 00:09:34.658
Oh. Jesus Christ!

50
00:10:00.028 --> 00:10:01.653
-Go!
-He won't jump. sir!

51
00:10:01.822 --> 00:10:04.657
-Don't listen!
-He's staying on the plane!

52
00:10:04.825 --> 00:10:07.530
He's not jumping.

53
00:10:07.703 --> 00:10:11.286
-He's okay! Go. sir! Go!
-All right!

54
00:10:11.457 --> 00:10:13.865
Son of a bitch.

55
00:10:27.182 --> 00:10:28.806
Where's the goddamn DZ?

56
00:10:29.267 --> 00:10:33.977
-Maybe three minutes on this bearing!
-We get lower. we won't need. . .

57
00:10:34.148 --> 00:10:36.140
. . .any frigging parachutes!

58
00:10:36.316 --> 00:10:39.436
-Slow down!
-We gotta get some altitude!

59
00:10:39.612 --> 00:10:42.566
They can't jump at this speed!

60
00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:44.982
We there?

61
00:10:45.952 --> 00:10:47.232
Oh. God!

62
00:10:47.411 --> 00:10:49.120
Oh. no!

63
00:10:52.041 --> 00:10:54.367
Let's go!

64
00:11:43.137 --> 00:11:46.008
-Flash.
-Shit.

65
00:11:46.182 --> 00:11:48.720
That's not the correct reply.
trooper.

66
00:11:48.893 --> 00:11:54.314
-l say ''flash.'' you say ''thunder. ''
-Yes. sir. Thunder. sir.

67
00:11:57.610 --> 00:12:00.066
Musette bag.

68
00:12:02.866 --> 00:12:07.160
Coach? Sir. it's Hall. sir.
l was on the basketball team.

69
00:12:07.329 --> 00:12:09.785
-Leg bag?
-Prop blast got it. sir.

70
00:12:09.957 --> 00:12:13.705
-And my radio and batteries with it.
-Mine too.

71
00:12:14.253 --> 00:12:17.373
Landed somewhere behind those trees.

72
00:12:18.883 --> 00:12:21.208
Okay.

73
00:12:22.095 --> 00:12:24.383
Follow me.

74
00:12:30.645 --> 00:12:32.971
To hell with that!

75
00:12:54.921 --> 00:12:57.542
Wait until they reload.

76
00:13:00.135 --> 00:13:02.258
Go.

77
00:13:05.307 --> 00:13:09.554
-Aren't you D Company?
-Able. sir.

78
00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:13.058
Means one of us
is in the wrong zone.

79
00:13:13.232 --> 00:13:16.482
Yeah. or both of us.

80
00:13:17.486 --> 00:13:21.567
-Do you have a weapon. sir?
-Just my knife.

81
00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:27.244
Do you have any idea
where we are. sir?

82
00:13:29.749 --> 00:13:31.825
Some.

83
00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:37.087
-So you're a radioman.
-Yes. sir.

84
00:13:37.257 --> 00:13:42.418
l was until l lost my radio on the jump.
l'll get chewed out for that.

85
00:13:42.596 --> 00:13:48.516
lf you were in my platoon. l'd say you
were a rifleman first. radioman second.

86
00:13:48.686 --> 00:13:53.846
Maybe you could say that to my leader.
When we find him. lf we find him.

87
00:13:54.025 --> 00:13:55.768
lt's a deal.

88
00:13:55.943 --> 00:14:01.614
First. l need your help. Locate some
landmarks to get our bearings.

89
00:14:01.783 --> 00:14:05.781
Keep your eyes peeled
for buildings. farmhouses. . .

90
00:14:05.954 --> 00:14:10.663
. . .bridges. roads. trees.

91
00:14:13.921 --> 00:14:16.791
l wonder if the rest
are as lost as we are.

92
00:14:16.965 --> 00:14:21.426
We're not lost. private.
We're in Normandy.

93
00:14:58.843 --> 00:15:03.920
-Who's that?
-Lt. Winters? ls that you?

94
00:15:07.978 --> 00:15:10.469
-Sit down. Any weapon?
-No. sir.

95
00:15:10.647 --> 00:15:14.977
l hit the prop blast. no more leg bag.
l have a knife and TNT.

96
00:15:15.152 --> 00:15:17.987
-The 82nd boys got M-1 s though.
-82nd?

97
00:15:18.155 --> 00:15:21.489
-Where are we?
-Sir. l saw a sign back there.

98
00:15:21.659 --> 00:15:24.660
lt said ''Sainte-Mère-Eglise. ''

99
00:15:30.918 --> 00:15:33.041
Flashlight?

100
00:15:33.421 --> 00:15:34.500
Raincoat?

101
00:15:34.672 --> 00:15:37.839
-You got a raincoat?
-Yeah. yeah.

102
00:16:00.741 --> 00:16:05.783
Seven kilometers from our objective.
Four hours from our deadline.

103
00:16:05.955 --> 00:16:09.905
So. we got a lot of walking
ahead of us.

104
00:16:10.085 --> 00:16:13.251
You'll stick with us
until we find your unit.

105
00:16:13.421 --> 00:16:15.295
Let's go.

106
00:16:15.465 --> 00:16:18.466
-Where are we going?
-Causeway 2. Utah Beach.

107
00:16:18.635 --> 00:16:22.419
Germans in the fields.
We need to clear it for our boys.

108
00:16:22.598 --> 00:16:27.593
Five of us won't secure a road.
That looey don't even have a weapon.

109
00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:30.724
l don't recall railroads
near our objective.

110
00:16:30.898 --> 00:16:34.267
This is the spur line.
parallel to the river.

111
00:16:34.444 --> 00:16:37.398
-We'll see a road and bridge.
-How do you know?

112
00:16:37.572 --> 00:16:40.988
Because l studied
the sand tables. all right?

113
00:16:44.496 --> 00:16:47.782
Probably a frigging train or--

114
00:16:47.958 --> 00:16:50.710
-Flash.
-Thunder.

115
00:16:51.461 --> 00:16:53.585
Lieutenant. is that you?

116
00:16:53.756 --> 00:16:55.499
-Malarkey.
-Sir. Sir.

117
00:16:55.674 --> 00:16:58.047
-Glad to see you. sir.
-Hey. fellas.

118
00:16:58.219 --> 00:17:00.757
-Everybody okay?
-Good to see you.

119
00:17:00.930 --> 00:17:02.305
-Guarnere?
-Sir.

120
00:17:02.473 --> 00:17:05.308
You and Hall up front.

121
00:17:05.476 --> 00:17:07.802
Who the hell is Hall?

122
00:17:40.263 --> 00:17:44.012
Lipton. Go. Guarnere.

123
00:18:05.289 --> 00:18:06.949
Wait for my command.

124
00:18:29.898 --> 00:18:32.271
Grenade!

125
00:18:49.502 --> 00:18:52.373
That's enough. Guarnere!

126
00:18:53.882 --> 00:18:57.547
-Everyone okay?
-Yes. sir.

127
00:18:58.178 --> 00:19:03.802
Next time l say wait for my command.
you wait for my command. sergeant.

128
00:19:03.976 --> 00:19:06.099
Yes. sir.

129
00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:16.145
Here you go. lieutenant.
Kraut weapon.

130
00:19:19.367 --> 00:19:22.203
Fine. Quaker.

131
00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:29.370
-What's that guy's problem?
-Gonorrhea.

132
00:19:29.545 --> 00:19:30.825
Really?

133
00:19:31.004 --> 00:19:34.421
His name. dummy.
Guarnere. gonorrhea. get it?

134
00:19:34.592 --> 00:19:37.758
So besides a shitty name.
what's his problem?

135
00:19:37.928 --> 00:19:40.846
None of your fucking business. cowboy.

136
00:19:41.015 --> 00:19:44.182
-All right. let's move out.
-Sir.

137
00:19:44.352 --> 00:19:46.677
Quietly.

138
00:20:03.706 --> 00:20:07.786
-You see him? He just sat there.
-He didn't have a weapon.

139
00:20:07.960 --> 00:20:12.124
-What's he gonna do. shout?
-Shouts at me for killing Krauts.

140
00:20:12.298 --> 00:20:15.216
He just wanted you to wait
for his command.

141
00:20:15.385 --> 00:20:18.339
Joe. he don't even drink.

142
00:20:35.489 --> 00:20:38.194
Lipton! Wynn!

143
00:21:17.366 --> 00:21:21.578
Anybody need supplies or ammo.
now's the time to get it.

144
00:21:25.792 --> 00:21:28.248
McDowell!
You okay?

145
00:21:28.420 --> 00:21:30.958
-Yes. sergeant.
-Well. let's go.

146
00:21:40.808 --> 00:21:45.055
l promised my brother l'd bring
him a Luger. l got first dibs.

147
00:21:45.229 --> 00:21:47.518
Check that one.

148
00:21:51.945 --> 00:21:54.317
-The Navy!
-Landings have started.

149
00:21:54.489 --> 00:21:56.612
-Move it out.
-Right on time.

150
00:21:56.783 --> 00:22:00.235
-Yeah? Tell that to him. cowboy.
-My name's Hall.

151
00:22:00.412 --> 00:22:03.496
-That so?
-Let's move out.

152
00:22:03.665 --> 00:22:07.366
-Learn to return his fire.
-lt ain't about you.

153
00:22:07.544 --> 00:22:11.376
-He heard his brother--
-Malarkey. shut your yap.

154
00:22:12.174 --> 00:22:16.338
His brother got it at Cassino.
Found out before we jumped.

155
00:22:29.526 --> 00:22:30.806
Morning. sir.

156
00:22:30.986 --> 00:22:34.022
-Battalion will be happy to see you.
-Where?

157
00:22:34.197 --> 00:22:35.740
At the farm. sir.

158
00:22:35.908 --> 00:22:39.692
Top of the morning to you. fellas.
Enjoying the war?

159
00:22:39.870 --> 00:22:42.242
Where you from. son?

160
00:22:42.998 --> 00:22:45.620
Eugene. Oregon.

161
00:22:45.793 --> 00:22:48.580
Eugene?
You gotta be kidding me.

162
00:22:48.754 --> 00:22:51.921
Popeye. did you hear this?
l'm from Astoria.

163
00:22:52.091 --> 00:22:55.674
-You don't say.
-Yeah. Orange Street.

164
00:22:55.845 --> 00:23:00.057
<i>-Why are you in a Kraut uniform?
-Volksdeutsche.</i>

165
00:23:00.225 --> 00:23:03.974
-Come again?
-My family answered the call.

166
00:23:04.146 --> 00:23:07.396
All true Aryans should return
to the Fatherland.

167
00:23:07.566 --> 00:23:10.437
-Joined up in '41 .
-You're shitting me.

168
00:23:10.611 --> 00:23:15.688
Hey. Malarkey! Stop fraternizing
with the enemy! Get over here!

169
00:23:15.866 --> 00:23:19.117
-What got you to Eugene?
-l was born in Eugene.

170
00:23:19.287 --> 00:23:20.745
Really?

171
00:23:33.385 --> 00:23:35.461
Popeye.

172
00:23:35.637 --> 00:23:38.093
Hey. Popeye!

173
00:23:39.057 --> 00:23:41.727
-Hey. Harry!
-Carry on.

174
00:23:41.894 --> 00:23:44.467
Easy Company.

175
00:23:45.064 --> 00:23:47.270
-Hey. Popeye.
-Good to see you.

176
00:23:47.441 --> 00:23:51.106
-This here's Hall. Able Company.
-Known as Cowboy.

177
00:23:51.279 --> 00:23:53.236
-You from Texas?
-Manhattan.

178
00:23:53.406 --> 00:23:55.363
Lt. Winters!

179
00:23:57.410 --> 00:24:00.411
-What's the holdup?
-Not sure.

180
00:24:01.164 --> 00:24:05.032
Five'll get you ten
it's got something to do with that.

181
00:24:05.210 --> 00:24:06.788
lt's good to see you.

182
00:24:06.962 --> 00:24:09.797
Yeah. you too. Buck.
What's the situation?

183
00:24:09.965 --> 00:24:13.963
Not good. Ninety percent of
the men are unaccounted for.

184
00:24:14.136 --> 00:24:18.086
-Lt. Meehan?
-No one's seen him.

185
00:24:18.265 --> 00:24:19.760
lf he is missing. . .

186
00:24:19.934 --> 00:24:24.430
. . .wouldn't that put you in line
to be the next commander of Easy?

187
00:24:27.275 --> 00:24:29.980
Hey. Lt. Speirs.

188
00:24:31.488 --> 00:24:34.323
How many men of Dog Company
got assembled?

189
00:24:34.491 --> 00:24:37.907
-Maybe 20.
-You the only officer that made it?

190
00:24:38.078 --> 00:24:40.117
So far.

191
00:24:40.288 --> 00:24:44.500
Still waiting for orders.
You got some cigarettes?

192
00:24:44.668 --> 00:24:46.827
Yeah.

193
00:24:48.464 --> 00:24:49.626
Keep the pack.

194
00:24:49.798 --> 00:24:52.468
Yeah. so l was in the plant in '39.

195
00:24:52.635 --> 00:24:57.593
l was at Monarch tooling propeller
shafts. What are the chances?

196
00:24:57.765 --> 00:25:01.763
You and me a hundred miles apart.
working at the same job.

197
00:25:01.936 --> 00:25:05.637
-Hey. Malark! We're waiting on you.
-Yeah. l'm coming.

198
00:25:05.815 --> 00:25:08.188
l gotta run.
l'll see you around.

199
00:25:08.360 --> 00:25:12.488
Yeah. see you around.

200
00:25:22.708 --> 00:25:24.665
<i>Zigaretten?</i>

201
00:25:26.462 --> 00:25:28.289
Here you go.

202
00:25:31.217 --> 00:25:33.293
<i>Danke.</i>

203
00:25:35.221 --> 00:25:36.419
<i>Danke.</i>

204
00:25:38.934 --> 00:25:40.725
Thank you.

205
00:25:50.154 --> 00:25:52.479
Shit.

206
00:25:52.656 --> 00:25:54.945
Easy Company?

207
00:25:55.117 --> 00:25:57.075
Easy?

208
00:25:57.453 --> 00:26:00.869
Hey. any of you guys know
where Easy Company is?

209
00:26:01.791 --> 00:26:04.282
-You seen Lt. Meehan?
-No. not yet.

210
00:26:04.460 --> 00:26:08.458
Well. Maj. Strayer wants
Easy Company's CO up front.

211
00:26:08.632 --> 00:26:10.790
-That means you. Dick.
-Come on.

212
00:26:10.967 --> 00:26:12.841
Son of a bitch.

213
00:26:15.222 --> 00:26:18.887
Hey. Malark. where's the best chow?

214
00:26:19.059 --> 00:26:21.431
ln Berlin.

215
00:26:25.691 --> 00:26:28.526
-Let's round them up.
-Okay. Get them.

216
00:26:28.694 --> 00:26:31.482
-And the MGs?
-l'd say around here. sir.

217
00:26:31.656 --> 00:26:33.981
But l can't be sure.

218
00:26:34.534 --> 00:26:39.279
There's Kraut 88s. Ahead
and to the right about 300 yards.

219
00:26:39.456 --> 00:26:43.323
Through the gardens. They're
between us and Causeway 2.

220
00:26:43.502 --> 00:26:45.909
Firing on the boys landing at Utah.

221
00:26:46.088 --> 00:26:48.164
-Can Easy handle it?
-Yes. sir.

222
00:26:48.340 --> 00:26:52.338
My guess is. they're doing
some terrible damage there.

223
00:26:52.845 --> 00:26:56.510
Does the major know we
only have 1 2 Easy Company men?

224
00:26:56.682 --> 00:26:58.556
No.

225
00:26:58.726 --> 00:27:03.139
The 88s we've heard
have been spotted in a field. . .

226
00:27:03.314 --> 00:27:05.639
. . .down the road a ways.

227
00:27:05.817 --> 00:27:08.569
Major Strayer wants us
to take them out.

228
00:27:08.736 --> 00:27:12.817
There are two guns that we know of.
firing on Utah Beach.

229
00:27:12.991 --> 00:27:15.564
Plan on a third and a fourth. . .

230
00:27:15.744 --> 00:27:19.409
. . .here and here.
The Germans are in the trenches. . .

231
00:27:19.581 --> 00:27:24.409
. . .with access to the entire battery.
Machine gun covering the rear.

232
00:27:24.586 --> 00:27:29.664
We establish a base of fire and move
under it with two squads of three.

233
00:27:30.009 --> 00:27:32.630
How many Krauts
you think we're facing?

234
00:27:32.803 --> 00:27:37.051
-No idea.
-No idea?

235
00:27:38.685 --> 00:27:42.433
We'll take some TNT along with us.
Despite the guns.

236
00:27:42.605 --> 00:27:44.729
-Your responsibility.
-Yes. sir.

237
00:27:44.900 --> 00:27:48.814
Liebgott. take the first machine gun.
with Petty A-gunner.

238
00:27:48.987 --> 00:27:52.902
Plesha. Hendrix. you take the other.
Who does that leave?

239
00:27:53.200 --> 00:27:57.328
Compton. Malarkey.
Toye. Guarnere. Okay.

240
00:27:57.496 --> 00:28:00.830
We'll be making the main assault.
Understood?

241
00:28:01.000 --> 00:28:02.245
Yes. sir.

242
00:28:02.418 --> 00:28:04.577
Let's pack it up. boys.

243
00:28:05.797 --> 00:28:08.751
Shouldn't you be with
the Able Company guys?

244
00:28:08.925 --> 00:28:11.463
See you around. Hall.

245
00:28:16.474 --> 00:28:21.896
Lipton. when you see we've captured
the first gun. l want your TNT fast.

246
00:28:22.064 --> 00:28:23.262
Yes. sir.

247
00:28:24.691 --> 00:28:28.143
Okay. Just weapons and ammo.
drop everything else.

248
00:28:28.320 --> 00:28:31.820
Got spare ammo in a pack
or a musette bag. bring it.

249
00:28:31.991 --> 00:28:36.155
Lieutenant. sir? l was wondering.
you need an extra hand?

250
00:28:36.329 --> 00:28:38.902
-Ain't you Sink's jeep driver?
-So?

251
00:28:39.082 --> 00:28:40.196
Oh. shit.

252
00:28:40.375 --> 00:28:42.498
What's your name. trooper?

253
00:28:42.669 --> 00:28:45.539
-Lorraine. sir.
-You're with me. Lorraine.

254
00:28:45.714 --> 00:28:47.956
-Compton. second squad.
-Yes. sir!

255
00:28:48.133 --> 00:28:52.427
All right. you heard the word.
Let's move! Let's move!

256
00:28:59.270 --> 00:29:01.096
Fire!

257
00:29:27.716 --> 00:29:29.792
Go.

258
00:29:31.679 --> 00:29:34.051
Three cannons.

259
00:29:40.062 --> 00:29:43.432
Petty. we've got enfilading fire.

260
00:29:43.608 --> 00:29:46.692
All right. let's go. Stay down.

261
00:29:58.791 --> 00:30:04.165
MG42s. l'll draw fire to the right of
the truck. Take two men and hit them. . .

262
00:30:04.338 --> 00:30:05.916
. . .from the left. Go.

263
00:30:06.090 --> 00:30:07.798
Right.

264
00:30:13.097 --> 00:30:17.843
Take Ranney. envelop right. give
covering fire. Lorraine. machine gun.

265
00:30:18.019 --> 00:30:20.510
Don't give away your position early.

266
00:30:20.689 --> 00:30:24.188
l want TNT as soon as we've
captured the first gun.

267
00:30:24.359 --> 00:30:26.601
-Go.
-Yes. sir.

268
00:30:44.047 --> 00:30:45.078
Go.

269
00:30:51.513 --> 00:30:54.086
l can't see nothing.

270
00:31:43.734 --> 00:31:46.060
Come on. Buck.

271
00:32:13.140 --> 00:32:14.421
Shit!

272
00:32:19.939 --> 00:32:21.599
Let's go! Let's go!

273
00:32:22.442 --> 00:32:24.066
Follow me!

274
00:32:33.161 --> 00:32:35.284
Come on!

275
00:32:37.124 --> 00:32:40.659
Fuck! My ass!

276
00:32:44.507 --> 00:32:46.583
Sorry. sir.

277
00:32:49.721 --> 00:32:51.713
Jesus Christ!

278
00:32:55.810 --> 00:32:57.554
Fucking jeep jockey.

279
00:32:57.729 --> 00:33:02.640
Shit! l'm sorry. sir.
l screwed up.

280
00:33:04.528 --> 00:33:06.686
Grenade!

281
00:33:06.864 --> 00:33:09.699
Joe! Toye! Roll on! Roll on!

282
00:33:09.867 --> 00:33:12.274
Get off!

283
00:33:13.954 --> 00:33:14.986
Shoot!

284
00:33:15.164 --> 00:33:17.370
One lucky bastard. Joe.

285
00:33:25.717 --> 00:33:29.715
Guarnere! Malarkey! Lorraine!
Secure that gun!

286
00:33:32.307 --> 00:33:35.842
-Compton. covering fire!
-Yes. sir!

287
00:33:47.156 --> 00:33:50.406
-Where you hit. Pop?
-l fucked up my ass. sir.

288
00:33:50.576 --> 00:33:52.818
Your ass?

289
00:33:54.831 --> 00:33:56.491
-Shit.
-How bad is it?

290
00:33:56.666 --> 00:34:02.502
l'm sorry. sir. l didn't mean to
fuck up. l don't think it's too bad.

291
00:34:03.465 --> 00:34:06.086
-Can you make it back yourself?
-Yes.

292
00:34:06.259 --> 00:34:08.086
Let's move out.

293
00:34:08.262 --> 00:34:12.805
Here we go. Drop your weapon. Pop.
drop your weapon. Come on.

294
00:34:12.975 --> 00:34:15.431
One. two. three!

295
00:34:15.603 --> 00:34:17.311
Get down. Dick. get down!

296
00:34:18.022 --> 00:34:20.643
Pop!

297
00:34:20.816 --> 00:34:23.272
Popeye! Get down!

298
00:34:24.445 --> 00:34:28.111
Winters! One o'clock!

299
00:34:28.283 --> 00:34:29.528
Grenade!

300
00:34:29.701 --> 00:34:34.612
Toye! Let's go! Get out of there!
Get out of there!

301
00:34:34.789 --> 00:34:36.948
Toye!

302
00:34:37.376 --> 00:34:40.495
-Joe!
-Jesus Christ.

303
00:34:40.671 --> 00:34:43.588
Fucking twice.

304
00:34:46.218 --> 00:34:49.136
Jesus Christ!

305
00:34:50.598 --> 00:34:53.089
Lorraine! Move! Go!

306
00:34:53.267 --> 00:34:55.556
Malark!

307
00:35:01.735 --> 00:35:04.819
Ranney!
Let's move! They got the first gun!

308
00:35:12.663 --> 00:35:15.415
-There's the second gun.
-Grenades first.

309
00:35:15.582 --> 00:35:17.492
-Then keep going. Go!
-Right.

310
00:35:24.008 --> 00:35:26.001
Okay.

311
00:35:27.136 --> 00:35:29.758
Go!

312
00:35:38.148 --> 00:35:39.690
Shut up.

313
00:35:39.858 --> 00:35:41.601
-No make dead.
-Shut up.

314
00:35:41.777 --> 00:35:45.525
-No make dead.
-Shut the fuck up!

315
00:35:50.911 --> 00:35:54.162
Toye. stay down.
Stay down!

316
00:35:54.332 --> 00:35:57.867
-Compton!
-All right. Cover for me.

317
00:36:00.004 --> 00:36:03.705
They're so confused.
they're firing on the third gun!

318
00:36:03.883 --> 00:36:06.457
Better blow this
before they realize it.

319
00:36:06.636 --> 00:36:11.678
-l'm gonna find Lipton.
-All right. Toye! Cover the lieutenant!

320
00:36:14.686 --> 00:36:17.438
-One of the dead Krauts has a Luger!
-So?

321
00:36:17.606 --> 00:36:20.228
Keep your head low. Petty.
Move it!

322
00:36:20.401 --> 00:36:25.277
