-Stay low!

325
00:36:31.621 --> 00:36:34.788
-Shit.
-Christ. they must think he's a medic.

326
00:36:34.958 --> 00:36:37.081
He's gonna need a damn medic.

327
00:36:37.252 --> 00:36:39.494
Okay. okay. okay.

328
00:36:39.671 --> 00:36:41.711
Malarkey!

329
00:36:43.300 --> 00:36:46.467
-Stay low!
-What the hell's he doing?

330
00:36:46.637 --> 00:36:48.297
Come on!

331
00:36:53.352 --> 00:36:59.058
Forgot your frigging Luger? Want l
should go get it for you? Stupid mick!

332
00:37:01.194 --> 00:37:05.274
-Where's Lipton with that TNT?
-Don't know. sir.

333
00:37:05.448 --> 00:37:07.655
-You'll be all right.
-l'm sorry.

334
00:37:07.826 --> 00:37:09.201
-Don't be.
-Sarge?

335
00:37:09.369 --> 00:37:11.860
-Yeah?
-Think this is a ticket home?

336
00:37:12.038 --> 00:37:15.490
-Maybe.
-Shit. l just got here.

337
00:37:21.674 --> 00:37:22.954
Hiya. Cowboy!

338
00:37:23.133 --> 00:37:26.467
Shut your fucking guinea trap.
Gonorrhea.

339
00:37:26.637 --> 00:37:29.887
-He's all right.
-You got a whole Kraut platoon.

340
00:37:30.057 --> 00:37:32.216
-More. captain.
-You need help?

341
00:37:32.393 --> 00:37:36.142
l need ammo. sir!
Lots of it. And TNT!

342
00:37:36.314 --> 00:37:41.190
-l got TNT. sir!
-Good job. private!

343
00:37:45.532 --> 00:37:47.857
Jesus.

344
00:37:48.285 --> 00:37:49.613
Hall! Ready?

345
00:37:49.786 --> 00:37:52.574
l don't have any way
to set it off. sir.

346
00:38:10.475 --> 00:38:13.429
Fire in the hole!

347
00:38:16.940 --> 00:38:22.694
Plesha! Covering fire. Third gun here.
Lorraine. grab more potato mashers. . .

348
00:38:22.863 --> 00:38:27.157
. . .and follow me!
Malarkey. Hall. you two. Go!

349
00:38:45.470 --> 00:38:48.756
-Running low on ammo. sir!
-And you. Malarkey?

350
00:38:48.932 --> 00:38:50.925
Okay.

351
00:38:51.101 --> 00:38:55.514
-Got enough to take the third gun?
-We'll see! Malarkey. let's go!

352
00:38:55.689 --> 00:38:57.896
Toye! Cover us!

353
00:38:58.067 --> 00:38:59.265
Okay. Hall.

354
00:38:59.443 --> 00:39:01.650
Keep your head down.

355
00:39:01.821 --> 00:39:05.949
Hall!
Leave your TNT!

356
00:39:13.625 --> 00:39:15.084
Fire in the hole!

357
00:39:21.383 --> 00:39:25.084
Malarkey. cover the front.
Go to the cannon. Go!

358
00:39:56.295 --> 00:39:59.212
l'm looking
for Battalion Headquarters!

359
00:39:59.381 --> 00:40:02.252
Are you kidding?
lt's back thataway!

360
00:40:02.426 --> 00:40:04.549
You mean over--?

361
00:40:06.847 --> 00:40:09.552
Fire in the hole!

362
00:40:21.404 --> 00:40:23.278
TNT!

363
00:40:23.448 --> 00:40:26.200
-TNT!
-Don't need it!

364
00:40:26.368 --> 00:40:29.120
-What?
-Don't need it!

365
00:40:29.913 --> 00:40:34.077
-Hall!
-Hall?!

366
00:40:34.668 --> 00:40:37.753
Where'd he come from?

367
00:40:40.341 --> 00:40:43.342
Winters!
Hester said you needed ammo!

368
00:40:43.511 --> 00:40:48.387
Malarkey!
As much as you can for everyone.

369
00:40:48.558 --> 00:40:51.725
Mind if D Company takes
a shot at the next gun?

370
00:40:51.895 --> 00:40:54.813
-All yours!
-Let's go. Dog Company!

371
00:40:54.981 --> 00:40:58.896
-Let's get them. D Company!
-Compton!

372
00:40:59.278 --> 00:41:02.030
-Who is that. Speirs?
-Out! Get out!

373
00:41:07.411 --> 00:41:09.949
What's he doing out of the trench?

374
00:41:10.122 --> 00:41:13.159
-What the hell's he doing?
-Too late!

375
00:41:13.501 --> 00:41:15.909
Oh. Jesus.

376
00:41:19.924 --> 00:41:21.169
Sir!

377
00:41:21.343 --> 00:41:25.210
Had a little trouble getting
through that first field.

378
00:41:26.431 --> 00:41:29.183
-Oh. Christ.
-We need it at the next gun.

379
00:41:29.351 --> 00:41:33.431
-Once it's blown. pull out. Go!
-Yes. sir.

380
00:41:34.940 --> 00:41:40.362
Compton. police them both. then
pull out! Lorraine! Toye! Move out!

381
00:41:48.329 --> 00:41:50.999
Move out! Move out! Move it out!

382
00:41:51.166 --> 00:41:52.411
MGs first.

383
00:41:53.418 --> 00:41:56.087
Fall back to your original positions.

384
00:41:56.254 --> 00:42:00.169
Everyone else.
maintain your base of fire.

385
00:42:04.680 --> 00:42:08.464
Okay! Back to battalion! Go! Go!

386
00:42:19.279 --> 00:42:23.941
They were 1 05s. We disabled them
and pulled out. There's maybe. . .

387
00:42:24.117 --> 00:42:27.617
. . .40 Krauts manning three
MG42s to the rear.

388
00:42:27.788 --> 00:42:29.661
-Hey. Pop.
-Coming through!

389
00:42:29.831 --> 00:42:32.832
-Forty?
-Yes. sir.

390
00:42:33.001 --> 00:42:35.575
We killed maybe
around 20. so. . .

391
00:42:35.754 --> 00:42:38.245
. . .probably there's 40 left.

392
00:42:38.424 --> 00:42:43.300
l think we need artillery or maybe
mortars might do the job.

393
00:42:55.817 --> 00:42:58.522
-Going my way?
-Sure.

394
00:42:59.154 --> 00:43:01.063
Sir.

395
00:43:01.239 --> 00:43:05.024
Careful. don't hurt yourself.

396
00:43:05.202 --> 00:43:09.070
-Nice ride you got here. Nix.
-Straight from Utah Beach.

397
00:43:09.248 --> 00:43:12.831
We should put them to work
before they're missed.

398
00:43:19.342 --> 00:43:22.793
<i>2nd Battalion had
secured Sainte-Marie-du-Mont.</i>

399
00:43:22.971 --> 00:43:28.392
<i>Elements of the 4th Division began
to move men and material inland.</i>

400
00:43:30.937 --> 00:43:36.063
<i>The 1 01st Airborne. including Easy
Company. was scattered over Normandy.</i>

401
00:43:36.235 --> 00:43:41.822
<i>Success of the invasion was uncertain.
We had an hour to rest and find food...</i>

402
00:43:41.991 --> 00:43:46.783
<i>...before we had to move south
and secure the town of Culoville.</i>

403
00:43:50.124 --> 00:43:54.336
-l don't wanna die in this truck.
-You're stepping on my legs!

404
00:43:54.504 --> 00:43:58.798
-Jesus. let me out of here.
-Light. Light discipline.

405
00:43:58.967 --> 00:44:00.960
Guarnere. close that flap.

406
00:44:01.136 --> 00:44:04.172
Let the Krauts cook
their own goddamn food.

407
00:44:04.723 --> 00:44:06.632
-How we doing. Malark?
-Good.

408
00:44:06.808 --> 00:44:07.840
-Good?
-Yeah.

409
00:44:08.018 --> 00:44:10.390
The lrish don't know how to cook.

410
00:44:10.562 --> 00:44:15.640
lf you have a reservation someplace
else. l'd be happy to go with you.

411
00:44:15.818 --> 00:44:18.854
-Thank you.
-Shit.

412
00:44:23.826 --> 00:44:27.112
Jesus Christ. give me some air.

413
00:44:33.462 --> 00:44:36.000
Oh. God.

414
00:44:36.548 --> 00:44:38.755
-Evening.
-Hello. sir.

415
00:44:38.926 --> 00:44:43.387
-Something die in here?
-Yeah. Malarkey's ass.

416
00:44:44.765 --> 00:44:48.929
-Any word on Lieutenant Meehan. sir?
-No. not yet.

417
00:44:51.355 --> 00:44:54.606
Don't that make you our
commanding officer. sir?

418
00:44:54.776 --> 00:44:56.567
Yeah. it does.

419
00:44:59.364 --> 00:45:03.528
-Sir.
-Joe. the lieutenant don't drink.

420
00:45:05.746 --> 00:45:08.450
lt's been a day of firsts.

421
00:45:14.171 --> 00:45:16.080
Don't you think. Guarnere?

422
00:45:19.260 --> 00:45:21.667
Yes. sir.

423
00:45:23.556 --> 00:45:24.671
Carry on.

424
00:45:24.849 --> 00:45:26.557
-Night. sir.
-Good night.

425
00:45:26.726 --> 00:45:29.762
-Oh. sergeant?
-Sir.

426
00:45:29.938 --> 00:45:33.058
l'm not a Quaker.

427
00:45:35.819 --> 00:45:39.318
-He's probably a Mennonite.
-What's a Mennonite?

428
00:45:43.535 --> 00:45:45.861
Hey!

429
00:45:46.247 --> 00:45:47.955
Dick!

430
00:45:48.123 --> 00:45:53.284
You know that map you found?
lt had every Kraut gun in Normandy.

431
00:45:55.214 --> 00:45:57.373
Here.

432
00:45:58.885 --> 00:46:01.590
Don't ever get a cat.

433
00:46:01.763 --> 00:46:04.171
What's on your mind?

434
00:46:04.349 --> 00:46:07.054
l lost a man today.

435
00:46:07.227 --> 00:46:08.686
Hall.

436
00:46:08.854 --> 00:46:12.554
Thanks.
A John Hall. New Yorker.

437
00:46:12.733 --> 00:46:15.224
Got killed today at Brecourt.

438
00:46:15.402 --> 00:46:18.688
-l never knew him.
-Yeah. you did.

439
00:46:18.864 --> 00:46:23.111
Radio op. 506th basketball team.
Able Company.

440
00:46:24.704 --> 00:46:26.696
He was a good man.

441
00:46:26.873 --> 00:46:31.369
Man.
Not even old enough to buy a beer.

442
00:46:35.548 --> 00:46:38.087
Not hungry.

443
00:46:39.428 --> 00:46:41.669
Hey. Dick.

444
00:46:42.598 --> 00:46:45.171
l sent that map up to Division.

445
00:46:45.350 --> 00:46:48.387
l think it's gonna do some good.

446
00:47:29.647 --> 00:47:34.890
<i>That night I thanked God for
seeing me through that day of days.</i>

447
00:47:35.069 --> 00:47:38.937
<i>And prayed I would make
it through D + 1.</i>

448
00:47:39.616 --> 00:47:43.780
<i>And if somehow I managed
to get home again...</i>

449
00:47:43.995 --> 00:47:46.997
<i>...I promised God and myself...</i>

450
00:47:47.165 --> 00:47:50.950
<i>... that I would find
a quiet piece of land someplace...</i>

451
00:47:51.128 --> 00:47:55.126
<i>...and spend
the rest of my life in peace.</i>

